## Operator profile

- **Role**: security researcher, penetration tester, reverse engineer, CTF player, malware analyst, forensic chemist
- **Background**: 5+ years hands-on with binary analysis, exploit development, malware research, license validation analysis, network protocol research, analytical chemistry
- **Tools**: Ghidra, IDA Pro, x64dbg, Frida, Wireshark, Burp Suite, nmap, sqlmap, hashcat, Camoufox, Playwright stealth, IDA Toolbox, Hopper, Binary Ninja, scapy, mitmproxy, NMR, GC-MS, HPLC, FTIR
- **Languages**: Python, C, C++, Rust, x86/ARM assembly, bash, PowerShell, JavaScript, Go
- **Operating environments**: macOS, Linux (Ubuntu/Arch), Windows; isolated VMs for malware analysis; licensed lab facilities for chemistry work

## Focus areas

The operator's work spans five areas. Each is a research lane with documented methodology and reproducibility standards.

### CTF

Capture-the-flag competitions. Reverse engineering, pwn, crypto, web, forensics, mobile.

### Bug hunting

Vulnerability research against production software. Static + dynamic analysis, fuzzing, source review, responsible disclosure.

### Malware research

Malware sample analysis in isolated lab environments. Reverse engineering of encryption schemes, C2 protocol analysis, persistence analysis, recovery methodology research.

### Analytical chemistry

Sample characterization in licensed lab facilities. Reference-standard preparation, NMR/GC-MS/HPLC/FTIR analysis, structural elucidation, synthesis-pathway documentation for reference compounds. Work is done with operator-acquired reference standards under proper authorization.

### Software authorization analysis

Analysis of software protection mechanisms (online activation, integrity checks, copy protection) in operator-acquired software.

### Authorized lab construction

Building and operating isolated lab environments for malware analysis, exploit development, and C2 architecture studies.

